1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,483
You walk into your living room, and it smells like fried fish.

2
00:00:05,533 --> 00:00:06,716
Nobody is cooking.

3
00:00:06,766 --> 00:00:07,949
Nobody ordered food.

4
00:00:07,999 --> 00:00:16,581
That smell might be the most expensive one you will ever ignore, because somewhere behind your walls, plastic could be melting.

5
00:00:16,631 --> 00:00:20,691
Today, seven warning signs your house sends before disaster strikes.

6
00:00:20,741 --> 00:00:24,802
And number one can turn deadly in a single evening.

7
00:00:26,152 --> 00:00:26,881
Number seven.

8
00:00:26,931 --> 00:00:28,440
A rumbling water heater.

9
00:00:28,490 --> 00:00:35,844
If your water heater pops, crackles, or rumbles like a giant coffee maker, that is not just old age.

10
00:00:35,894 --> 00:00:45,586
A layer of sediment has built up at the bottom of the tank, and water trapped underneath it is boiling and exploding its way out.

11
00:00:45,636 --> 00:00:51,431
That means overheating, wasted energy, and in the worst case, a tank that fails completely.

12
00:00:51,481 --> 00:00:54,938
Flushing the tank once a year usually fixes it.

13
00:00:54,988 --> 00:00:57,666
Ignoring it for years means replacing it.

14
00:00:59,016 --> 00:00:59,696
Number six.

15
00:00:59,746 --> 00:01:02,251
Bubbling or peeling paint on the ceiling.

16
00:01:02,301 --> 00:01:05,172
Paint does not bubble because it is bored.

17
00:01:05,222 --> 00:01:11,377
Water is collecting behind it, from a leaking roof, a cracked pipe, or an overflowing bathroom upstairs.

18
00:01:11,427 --> 00:01:17,583
By the time you can see a bubble, the leak has usually been running for a while.

19
00:01:17,633 --> 00:01:20,503
Do not just pop it and forget it.

20
00:01:20,553 --> 00:01:28,534
Find the source and fix it fast, because wet ceilings grow mold, and soggy drywall eventually comes down all on its own.

21
00:01:29,884 --> 00:01:30,562
Number five.

22
00:01:30,612 --> 00:01:32,381
A breaker that keeps tripping.

23
00:01:32,431 --> 00:01:37,112
Once in a while is fine, that is the breaker doing its job.

24
00:01:37,162 --> 00:01:46,937
But if the same switch flips every week, your house is telling you a circuit is overloaded, or a wire is loose somewhere it should not be.

25
00:01:46,987 --> 00:01:53,487
Do not just flip it back and move on, and never, ever swap it for a bigger breaker.

26
00:01:53,537 --> 00:01:57,126
That silences the messenger, and lets the wiring slowly cook.

27
00:01:57,176 --> 00:01:58,582
Call an electrician instead.

28
00:01:59,932 --> 00:02:00,652
Number four.

29
00:02:00,702 --> 00:02:04,119
Stair step cracks in your brick or block walls.

30
00:02:04,169 --> 00:02:08,742
Hairline cracks happen in every house, and most of them are harmless.

31
00:02:08,792 --> 00:02:16,831
But cracks that climb through the mortar in a staircase pattern mean one side of your foundation is moving, or sinking.

32
00:02:16,881 --> 00:02:19,143
Watch for the supporting cast too.

33
00:02:19,193 --> 00:02:24,151
Doors that suddenly stick, windows that will not close, and floors that slope.

34
00:02:24,201 --> 00:02:30,314
If they all show up together, get a foundation inspection before the repair price gets scary.

35
00:02:31,664 --> 00:02:32,451
Number three.

36
00:02:32,501 --> 00:02:34,124
A yellow pilot light.

37
00:02:34,174 --> 00:02:39,564
The flame in your gas furnace or water heater should burn crisp blue.

38
00:02:39,614 --> 00:02:47,514
If it burns lazy yellow or orange, the gas is not burning completely, and incomplete burning produces carbon monoxide.

39
00:02:47,564 --> 00:02:52,953
A gas you cannot see, cannot smell, and cannot survive in high doses.

40
00:02:53,003 --> 00:03:00,066
Black soot around the appliance, and constant condensation on nearby windows, are parts of the same warning.

41
00:03:00,116 --> 00:03:04,250
Get a carbon monoxide detector, and get the appliance serviced.

42
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:06,389
Number two.

43
00:03:06,439 --> 00:03:08,066
That fried fish smell.

44
00:03:08,116 --> 00:03:17,290
Electrical wiring is wrapped in plastic insulation, and when connections overheat, that plastic starts to melt, and melting insulation smells like fish.

45
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:30,288
If the smell is strongest near an outlet, a switch, or your breaker panel, and it comes and goes with certain appliances, treat it as a fire alarm that arrived early.

46
00:03:30,338 --> 00:03:34,900
Unplug what you can, and call an electrician the same day.

47
00:03:34,950 --> 00:03:38,254
House fires often send this exact invitation first.

48
00:03:39,604 --> 00:03:40,674
And number one.

49
00:03:40,724 --> 00:03:42,541
The smell of rotten eggs.

50
00:03:42,591 --> 00:03:49,637
Natural gas has no smell at all, so gas companies add that stink on purpose, to save your life.

51
00:03:49,687 --> 00:04:01,213
If your home suddenly smells like rotten eggs, do not turn any lights on or off, do not use your phone inside, and do not start the car in the garage.

52
00:04:01,263 --> 00:04:02,707
One spark is enough.

53
00:04:02,757 --> 00:04:09,802
Open a door on your way out, walk everyone outside, and call the gas company from a safe distance.

54
00:04:09,852 --> 00:04:10,922
Every minute matters.

55
00:04:12,272 --> 00:04:16,134
Here is the rule that ties all seven together.

56
00:04:16,184 --> 00:04:18,742
Houses almost never fail without warning.

57
00:04:18,792 --> 00:04:24,827
They whisper first, through smells, sounds, and cracks, and disasters happen when nobody listens.

58
00:04:24,877 --> 00:04:25,696
Quick recap.

59
00:04:25,746 --> 00:04:27,869
A rumbling heater means sediment.

60
00:04:27,919 --> 00:04:30,042
Bubbling paint means a leak.

61
00:04:30,092 --> 00:04:32,650
A restless breaker means bad wiring.

62
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:35,258
Staircase cracks mean a moving foundation.

63
00:04:35,308 --> 00:04:37,866
A yellow flame means carbon monoxide.

64
00:04:37,916 --> 00:04:40,474
A fishy smell means melting wires.

65
00:04:40,524 --> 00:04:45,690
And rotten eggs mean gas, get out first, and ask questions later.

66
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:51,775
Walk through your home this weekend and check all seven, it takes ten minutes.

67
00:04:51,825 --> 00:04:57,425
Then share this with someone who owns a house, and subscribe for more.

68
00:04:57,475 --> 00:05:02,206
Stay safe, stay curious, and see you in the next one.
